                "word": "concretization",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3b8a6fa3-32dd-48cf-a7d2-db407dbb7739",
                        "entry_id": "76a3f89a-8fc1-3876-bcc7-ed581b368aa8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "concretizations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bad725a8-67c6-36f4-9027-e454a4cc57f4",
                        "entry_id": "76a3f89a-8fc1-3876-bcc7-ed581b368aa8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The process of concretizing a general principle or idea by delineating, particularizing, or exemplifying it."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14ed214b-2f1d-4c33-9333-a562e80fb4aa",
                                "sense_id": "bad725a8-67c6-36f4-9027-e454a4cc57f4",
                                "text": "There are certain fields in general economics that are at present not so much in need of a broadening of the theoretical basis as in need of a minute working-out and concretization."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17567d4c-c5b9-44ba-9f4e-e30e67401df3",
                                "sense_id": "bad725a8-67c6-36f4-9027-e454a4cc57f4",
                                "text": "[Law] proceeds from the general (abstract) to the individual (particular); it is a process of increasing individualization and concretization."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "24b00efe-3d62-395e-8bc1-d20a12b7dc59",
                        "entry_id": "76a3f89a-8fc1-3876-bcc7-ed581b368aa8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something specific which is the result of a process of concretizing a general principle or idea."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d28a8b42-d42a-463c-9c12-565a0507c693",
                                "sense_id": "24b00efe-3d62-395e-8bc1-d20a12b7dc59",
                                "text": "This movement gave Sherman his first image—a roller skate—a concretization of pure motion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bc5e8a1-e2c7-4757-9d0c-9d6b6db0b589",
                                "sense_id": "24b00efe-3d62-395e-8bc1-d20a12b7dc59",
                                "text": "Vodicka's reception history is an empirical study of the post-genesis fortunes of literary works as attested in recorded concretizations (diaries, memoirs, letters, critical reviews, and essays)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f205a336-1aed-3243-ae3d-47c1d2c37932",
                        "entry_id": "76a3f89a-8fc1-3876-bcc7-ed581b368aa8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An inability to generalize or perform abstraction accompanied by excessive concentration on specific details, as in a mental disorder or in cognition by children."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "022c12f5-7491-4791-999d-8b42869e5f8b",
                                "sense_id": "f205a336-1aed-3243-ae3d-47c1d2c37932",
                                "text": "Another [patient] commented on the fact that the consultant had referred to two of them as \"boys\" in the demonstration. The concretization of a schizophrenic is exemplified here. One man thought this word meant that the consultant, in order \"to keep things on the level of boy-girl, wanted everyone else to consider her as a girl, so the boys and girls could communicate.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
